MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_001: Promised One! We found ourselves thrilled by your\nhandling of that last battle! 
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_002: Truly ingenious, how you maneuvered all the\nforces at your disposal!
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_003: Clearly, the spirits of nature favor you as a ruler,\ngranting you their blessed protection.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_004: <NCA>"I'm not a ruler. Not in any way."
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_005: Ah, what modesty. But you embody promise and\nheroism, and what better qualities for a ruler?
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_006: Further, your voice commands with clarity, and in\nyour humble way, you draw forces to your side.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_007: We ourselves could never measure up to your\nsuperlative standard.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_008: <NCA>"This really weighs on you, doesn't it?"
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_009: Hahaha! Does it? We suppose it does! Well, the\nking of Brigid has unexpected depths!
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_010: Moreover, we have now been in Dagda for years,\noften perceived as a mere young wanderer.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_011: <NCA>"Why haven't you gone home?"
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_012: <NCB>"Why have you stayed for our fight?"
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_013: <ACA>We have...unfinished business here.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_014: <ACB>We came to Dagda originally out of interest for\nBrigid—to better guide its fate.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_015: Our duty is to the spirit islands, every single one\nof them, with all their beauty.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_016: But this continent—our neighbor—is suffering such\nshakes and shocks.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_017: We have hoped for a swift end to this, that our\nsmaller nation would be safe.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_018: So, this is also our battle, though on foreign soil.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_019: But we now fight for so much more.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_020: This land has taught us much and brought us many\nfriends. Among them you, Promised One.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_021: We ourselves owe Dagda a great debt.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_022: So we feel this not as a king...
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_023: We feel this at our core! As Penrose Peregrinus!
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_024: <NCA>"Your loyalty moves me."
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_025: Ah! Nothing could tear us away now—not our father,\nnot the Fang... Nothing!
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_A_026: We will fight by your side to the last!
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_001: Promised One! Thank goodness you've returned!
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_002: This must be the work of the spirits! We are all so\nfortunate to have their protection.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_003: We are grateful to you, spirits of Dagda!
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_004: <NCA>"You just ran up to me...really fast."
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_005: Oh, we have been no stranger to running of late.\nYou see, we have waited in this city for you.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_006: Many from Brigid have come, trying to serve our\nroyal person. We have had to stay on the run!
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_007: Honestly, as if they haven't any notion how long\nwe have been coping on our own here in Dagsion.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_008: We were just now bobbing and weaving through\nback alleys quite deftly, avoiding our servants.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_009: We know the capital so well! But that is what\nbrought us here to you in breathless haste.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_010: We have heard many tales about Dagda's temple\nand guessed you would come back here in time.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_011: <NCA>"You stayed for my sake. Thank you."
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_012: <NCB>"Impressive as ever...Peppe."
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_013: <ACA>Th-thank you? Oh, no, no... It was our pleasure.\nBut we have had to put kingly things aside.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_014: <ACB>Hahaha! Indeed, we ARE very us! Really though,\nit was nothing at all!
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_015: *sigh* But now, we must find our servants. They will\nbe worrying themselves into quite a state.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_016: The wars are over. A joyous event.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_017: We will always hold the people of Dagda close to\nour heart—with the people of Brigid.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_018: We vowed to stay in this land until the day that\npeace reigned again.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_019: Hmm.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_020: But the time has come. We must return home.\nOur own people need us.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_021: <NCA>"Is this goodbye?"
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_022: We do not wish that. Not at all.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_023: So, we must ask, Promised One... Do you intend to\ncontinue on, helping the people of the world?
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_024: <NCA>"Yes."
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_028: 
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_025: <RSDS>We hoped you would say that. Then come with\nus—to the land where we are king.
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_026: Do it for Dagda, for Brigid, for the world...
MID_SE_Ism_Pep_S_027: The king of the spirit islands and the world's\nPromised One! We are more...together!